Note that this program shows off the advanced Plainspeak features.
To find the factorial with n, do the following.
If n is less than or equal to 1, start doing the following.
Return 1.
Stop doing that.
Subtract 1 from n and call it m.
Call find the factorial with m and call it sub_result.
Multiply n and sub_result and call it the result.
Return the result.
That is the end of find the factorial.
Call find the factorial with 6 and call it answer.
Print Six factorial is:.
Print the answer.
Let the fruits be an empty list.
Add apple to the fruits.
Add banana to the fruits.
Add cherry to the fruits.
Print All the fruits:.
For each fruit in the fruits, start doing the following.
Print fruit.
Stop doing that.
Let the size be the length of the fruits.
Print The number of fruits is:.
Print the size.
Let a be 8.
Let b be 3.
If a is greater than 5 and b is less than 10, start doing the following.
Print Both conditions held at once.
Stop doing that.
Find the remainder of 17 divided by 5 and call it r.
Raise 2 to the power of 8 and call it p.
Print The remainder and the power were:.
Print r.
Print p.
Make plainspeak uppercase and call it shout.
Print shout.
